marta (docs): Opened PR for audit-log migration guide and SDK snippets: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/512
Please review SOC2 language and retention examples.

docs-ci-bot: CI: docs build passed — 2 warnings (link-checker).

ryan (security): Quick Q: SOC2 says 'reasonable retention' — do we standardize on 90 days for audit logs or state configurable? Need a concise sentence for policy.

leo (legal): Prefer 'retention configurable by customer; default 90 days for hosted'. Avoid 'indefinite'. Add exportability note: customers must be able to export audit data in machine-readable form for audits.

marta (docs): OK will update wording. Also need an SDK example showing redaction before sending logs and the new header `X-RW-Retain-Until` — can someone add a small python/node snippet? Also flag any technical constraints (max header length?)

sam (eng): Adding node + python snippets inline. For redaction we suggest regex + whitelist approach. Example:

```js
// Node.js sample
const auditEvent = { user_email: "user@example.com", action: "model_call", prompt: "card 4242 4242 4242 4242", credit_card: "4242424242424242" };
// simple redact: mask common card patterns
const redactCard = s => s.replace(/\b(?:\d{13,16})\b/g, "[REDACTED]");
auditEvent.prompt = redactCard(auditEvent.prompt);
auditEvent.credit_card = "[REDACTED]";

fetch("https://api.redwood.com/v1/audit_log", {
  method: "POST",
  headers: {
    "Authorization": "Bearer $TOKEN",
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "X-RW-Retain-Until": new Date(Date.now()+90*24*3600*1000).toISOString()
  },
  body: JSON.stringify(auditEvent)
});
```

```py
# Python sample
import requests, re, datetime

event = {"user_id": "u123", "prompt": "please reset my password 1234", "result": "ok"}
# redact password-like tokens
event["prompt"] = re.sub(r"(?i)password\b.*", "[REDACTED]", event["prompt"]) 
headers = {
  "Authorization": "Bearer ...",
  "Content-Type": "application/json",
  "X-RW-Retain-Until": (datetime.datetime.utcnow()+datetime.timedelta(days=90)).isoformat()+"Z"
}
requests.post("https://api.redwood.com/v1/audit_log", json=event, headers=headers)
```

marta (docs): Awesome, will add both. @leo can you confirm the export sentence: "Customers may export audit logs in machine-readable formats for compliance reviews; retention is configurable per-tenant (default 90 days for hosted)" ?

leo (legal): Fine but say "default 90 days for hosted deployments" and add "customers are responsible for their own retention policy when self-hosting."

ryan (security): Two small technical notes:
- we should recommend server-side redaction as best practice, not client-only
- add note about max payload size for audit endpoint (128KB currently)

marta (docs): Adding security and legal tweaks now. I'll push an updated PR description and ping everyone when done. Thanks :rocket:

